{
  "_README": [
    "THE PAINT. One entry per palette. Each has a `dark` and a `light` block,",
    "because the site has a scheme toggle and a one-mode palette would half-work.",
    "",
    "AN ABSENT KEY INHERITS. A PRESENT KEY WINS.",
    "Leave a token out and it comes from the palette named in `inherits`, then",
    "from `_base`. So a palette that only changes its neutrals lists only its",
    "neutrals -- see `uritp-granite`, which keeps the house blue by not",
    "mentioning it.",
    "",
    "`_base` is the safety net and must stay COMPLETE. Never point a theme at it.",
    "",
    "Values may be oklch() or hex; the contrast gate parses both. oklch is the",
    "house default because it is the one you can nudge by hand: the three numbers",
    "are lightness, chroma (0 = grey), hue angle (90 = warm, 250 = cool).",
    "",
    "Full reference: theme/README.md"
  ],

